osol Modelling Faculty of Physics Aug 20, 2026 Tenure Track Professorships Faculty of Physics Aug 20, 2026 Tenure-Track Professorship in Security, Society and the Global East Tenure-Track Professorship in Security, Society and the Global East Faculty of Social Sciences Aug 20, 2026 Tenure Track Professorships Faculty of Social Sciences Aug 20, 2026 Tenure-Track Professorship in Medieval Latin Tenure-Track Professorship in Medieval Latin Faculty of Philological and Cultural Studies Aug 20, 2026 Tenure Track Professorships Faculty of Philological and Cultural Studies Aug 20, 2026 Tenure Track Professorships at the University of Vienna Manuela Baccarini Vice-rector for research and international affairs on tenure track professorships at the University of Vienna. We offer a dynamic research environment attractive working conditions in a city with a high quality of life career development opportunities to tenured (full) professorships The ideal candidates will be a leader in their field and share our enthusiasm for excellence in research and teaching has an outstanding publication record and is internationally recognized holds a doctoral degree/PhD and has at least two years of international research experience Open positions Analytical Chemistry Caucasus Studies Church History (History of the Reformation and of Protestantism) Complex Systems Science in Microbiome Research Economic Anthropology Foundations of Machine Learning in Finance Gene-Culture Coevolution Islamic Theology Italian Literary, Cultural, Media Studies Japanese Politics Legal Anthropology Modern Methods in Drug Synthesis Molecular Disease Mechanisms National Socialism and the Holocaust in Austria and Europe Nucleic Acid Chemistry Organic Chemistry Sociology of Markets and Organizations Open positions @University of Vienna Current vacancies in the category ‘tenure track professorship’ Open tenure track position Complex Systems Science in Microbiome Research Open positions Analytical Chemistry Caucasus Studies Church History (History of the Reformation and of Protestantism) Complex Systems Science in Microbiome Research Economic Anthropology Foundations of Machine Learning in Finance Gene-Culture Coevolution Islamic Theology Italian Literary, Cultural, Media Studies Tenure Track professorships currently open at the University of Vienna. Japanese Politics Legal Anthropology Modern Methods in Drug Synthesis Molecular Disease Mechanisms National Socialism and the Holocaust in Austria and Europe Nucleic Acid Chemistry Organic Chemistry Sociology of Markets and Organizations Complex Systems Science in Microbiome Research Sociology of Markets and Organizations Foundations of Machine Learning in Finance Legal Anthropology Economic Anthropology Japanese Politics Complex Systems Science in Microbiome Research Sociology of Markets and Organizations Foundations of Machine Learning in Finance Legal Anthropology Economic Anthropology Japanese Politics Complex Systems Science in Microbiome Research Sociology of Markets and Organizations Foundations of Machine Learning in Finance Legal Anthropology Economic Anthropology Japanese Politics Career @University of Vienna Tenure track professors are hired as assistant professors on a six-year fixed-term contract. Tenure and promotion to associate professor are contingent upon positive evaluation within the first six years of employment. Associate professors with outstanding achievements can be promoted to full professor in a university-wide competitive procedure. The University of Vienna is an equal opportunity employer and values diversity. Given equal qualifications, preference will be given to female applicants. Karin O. Karin O. is tenure-track professor for the analysis of biomolecules at the Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences. In the clip she gives insights into her research activities at the Faculty of Life Sciences at #UniVienna. Meet Lukas S., tenure-track professor in machine learning at the Department for Statistics and Operations Research at University of Vienna. Dive into the video where he shares his excitement for clear mathematical truths and reveals how his role empowers him to carve out his unique research path. Appointment procedure for tenure track professorships Tenure track professorships are advertised internationally. Applications are subject to comparative international review and appointments are made based on the recommendations of a panel of experts chaired by the vice-rector for research. A qualification agreement stipulating the terms of the tenure position is offered at the start of employment. Fulfilment of the agreement leads to a permanent employment contract as tenured associate professor. Find more information on the intranet (log in with the u:account userID) Analytical Chemistry Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. Opens in a new tab. About us Career UniVie University of Vienna Legal Notice Imprint Privacy Policy Accessibility Cookie Consent Manager Jobs in Administration & Organisation Administration & Organisation (E) Data & Library Services (E) Facility Management (E) Finance & Controlling Communications & Marketing Coordination & Management HR IT Laboratory & Technology Research & Teaching Services (E) Jobs in Research & Teaching Work & Study - Start your career predoctoral postdoctoral Tenure Track Professorships All vacancies All Vacancies × Cookie Consent Manager When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Required Cookies These cookies are required to use this website and can't be turned off. Required Cookies Show More Details Required Cookies Provider Description Enabled SAP as service provider We use the following session cookies, which are all required to enable the web